# Privacy Policy

After every **feature**, **bugfix**, or **enhancement**, check whether `POLICY.md` still matches what the product does. The website `/privacy` route renders that file — update `POLICY.md` only; do not duplicate the text in Svelte.

## When to update

Required if the change does any of:

- collects, stores, or uploads new data (accounts, matches, replays, screenshots, process names, logs, comments)
- publishes new player or match data on the website or API
- adds or changes a third-party integration (Steam, Relic, Twitch, ElevenLabs, Cloudflare, …)
- changes what an account stores (email, Steam ID, avatar) or how fair play works
- starts using data for a new purpose (analytics, marketing, sharing)

Then: edit `POLICY.md`, set a new **Effective date** if the change is material, and keep `/privacy` and in-app privacy links working (including Tauri `opener:allow-open-url` for `https://coh1stats.com/*`).

## When to skip

- UI, copy, styling, refactors, or Cursor rules with no data-handling change
- The policy already describes the behavior

## Voice

Stay accurate. We do not store sensitive personal data. The only personal contact detail we might have is an email, and only if the user replaces the generated `@fknoobs.com` placeholder. Game identifiers (Steam ID, alias, match stats) are CoH/Relic/Steam data, not real-life identity. Do not claim we collect “no personal data” if we still store game or account fields.

```markdown
# ❌ BAD — ship fair-play uploads / a new API field and leave POLICY.md unchanged

# ✅ GOOD — POLICY.md lists the new data, purpose, and whether it is public or local-only
```
